    "prompt": "There is a bug in the matplotlib library where calling get_backend() clears figures from the global figure manager (Gcf.figs) if they were created inside an rc_context. This issue causes unexpected removal of figures, which in turn leads to errors such as plt.close(fig2) failing because the figure cannot be found. The expected behavior is that figures created under an rc_context remain intact and accessible after the context is exited. The fix should ensure that the backend parameter is not reset when using rc_context, thus preserving the state of figures.",
    "hint_texts": "Focus on modifying the rc_context function in the matplotlib initialization code. The implementation should make a copy of the existing rcParams, then remove the 'backend' key from this copy so that it is not restored when the context ends. Use the provided reproduction code as guidance to understand how the removal of figures occurs and verify that the backend setting remains unchanged after get_backend() is called.",
    "entrypoint": "File: lib/matplotlib/__init__.py; Function: rc_context. Modify the code block starting around lines 1059 to 1089 to create a dictionary copy of rcParams and delete the 'backend' key from it before proceeding.",
